\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$" "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$"] [:db/cas 17592186319250 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x(x+2)}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x(x+2)}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319251 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+3}{(x-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319253 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319254 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8-x}{x(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}