:question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-7}^{\\sqrt{3}-6}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+12x+37}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-7}^{\\sqrt{3}-6}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+12x+37}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319267 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{4-1/\\sqrt{3}}^{5}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319268 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{5}^{5+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}-10x+26}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319269 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319270 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{3x+7}{{x}^{2}+8x+16}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319271 :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$ using integration by parts. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186319271 :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{5}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{5}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I \\\\ 6I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{6}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{6}-{0}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{243}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's denote the indefinite integral by $$\n\\displaystyle I=\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{5}⁡x & \\,⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4x} & \\,⇒\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{4x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{5}⁡x)\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)-\\int \\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5{ln}^{4}⁡x}{x}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5\\int \\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $I.$ We can ignore the constant of integration in this case, because it is insignificant for further evaluation of the definite integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4}-5I \\\\ 6I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{4} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{ln}^{6}⁡x}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate our definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{ln}^{5}⁡x}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡x)\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({ln}^{6}⁡({e}^{3})-{ln}^{6}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}((3\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)^{6}-{0}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}({3}^{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{243}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186319274 :question/problem "What is the value of $h(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+{e}^{\\,t-1}\\,j+\\sqrt[4]{t+15}\\,sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)\\,k$ at $t=1?$\n\n$h(1)=$\n{{field-1}} $i\\,+\\,$\n\n{{field-2}} $j\\,+\\,$\n\n{{field-3}} $k$" "What is the value of $$\n\\displaystyle h(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+{e}^{\\,t-1}\\,j+\\sqrt[4]{t+15}\\,sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)\\,k\n$$ at $t=1?$\n\n$h(1)=$\n{{field-1}} $i\\,+\\,$\n\n{{field-2}} $j\\,+\\,$\n\n{{field-3}} $k$"] [:db/cas 17592186319279 :question/problem "